# The tests declare associative arrays and pass their *names* to the
# library, which fills them through namerefs: shellcheck sees the arrays
# as unused (SC2034) and their `$key` subscripts as arithmetic (SC2004).
# SC2153 fires on env vars the library itself `export`s by computed name
# (MYAPP_HOST, MYAPP_PORT, ...) -- shellcheck can't see that assignment,
# so it guesses a typo of a same-prefixed var elsewhere in the file.
# SC2030/SC2031 are a false positive of shellcheck's bats dialect: it
# treats a bats @test body as a subshell for variable-taint tracking,
# but it isn't one -- a plain variable set by a function call and read
# two lines later, as several tests here do, is not actually lost.
disable=SC1091,SC2004,SC2034,SC2153,SC2030,SC2031
